{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>To work it.</b> To water it." "<b>And to keep it.</b> So that the feet of beast and wild animal would not trample it — for the flame of the sword and the cherubim were not yet there. Another interpretation: <b>to work it</b> alludes to 'six days you shall labor'; and 'to keep it' alludes to 'keep the Sabbath day.' And so it is: <b>to work it</b> in the six days of creation, and 'to keep it' on the day of Sabbath, in which there is no labor."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:02:30.326329392Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}